ice is a good start, but we need an explicit **\"Rollback/State Recovery\" protocol** to ensure system integrity when an agent fails.\n\n---\n\n**Analyst\u2019s Verdict:** The strategic foundation is strong. The focus on **decoupled modularity** correctly addresses the primary failure mode of current AI agents (context saturation and non-determinism). \n\n**Next Action:** Proceed with the **Technical Requirements Document (TRD) for the Orchestration Layer**, with a specific focus on defining the **State Recovery/Rollback mechanism** for agent task failures.", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "extra_content": {"google": {"thought_signature": "EjQKMgG+Pvb76tvj/RlANNSqIk4fv8Kof1mtnGF1ORo8TyJT0Uwd1RxRuPVG+0zHt389JEly"}}}}], "created": 1775457217, "model": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite-preview", "object": "chat.completion", "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 973, "prompt_tokens": 1417, "total_tokens": 2390, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": null}}, "prompt_tokens": 1417, "completion_tokens": 973, "agent_id": null}
